🚀 Latest Improvements

Since the last update, the project has been significantly improved in terms of architecture, stability, and production readiness.

🔧 Navigation & App Stability

Refactored MainNavHost to follow a more scalable and maintainable navigation structure.

Introduced:

cleaner route handling

encoded navigation arguments (e.g., category)

safer navigation extensions

Fixed startup issues related to improper ViewModel initialization.

Ensured proper lifecycle-aware state handling using collectAsStateWithLifecycle.

🧠 ViewModel & State Management

Improved ViewModel integration with Hilt:

Added proper @HiltViewModel usage

Ensured dependency injection consistency across layers

Refactored state handling:

Introduced a more stable CartUiState

Used combine + StateFlow for reactive UI updates

Optimized UI reactivity and reduced unnecessary recompositions.

💉 Dependency Injection Improvements

Strengthened DI setup using Hilt:

Clean separation of responsibilities in AppModule

Proper scoping with @Singleton

Ensured:

database

DAO

repositories
are injected in a production-ready manner

🗄️ Data Layer Enhancements

Improved interaction between:

Room Database

CartRepository

ProductRepository

Ensured a more predictable data flow:

local data + UI state synchronization

Prepared architecture for easy backend integration.

🧩 Code Quality & Structure

Further improved project modularization:

cleaner separation between feature, domain, and data

Increased readability and maintainability:

better naming conventions

reduced duplication

Followed a more production-level code organization style.

🎯 UI & UX Improvements

Improved:

bottom navigation behavior

cart badge updates

screen transitions

Better handling of:

padding

system UI (status bar & navigation bar styling)

More consistent visual behavior across screens.

🧪 Stability & Debugging

Fixed critical issues related to:

app startup crashes

ViewModel lifecycle

navigation state

Improved debugging workflow using Logcat and structured filtering.

📈 Current Development Level

This project has evolved from a simple UI prototype into a structured, scalable Android application with:

real architecture decisions

lifecycle-aware state management

dependency injection

local persistence

reusable UI system

It is now moving towards a production-ready level application.

